Parent UQ in agentic inference setups is a paradigm shift from point-wise estimates to sequential dynamics models.
Evaluation of predictive uncertainty has been conducted by measuring the informativeness of uncertainty estimates when predicting incorrectness, which becomes insufficient for multi-faceted evaluation in agentic LLM setups. A new protocol is envisioned that integrates multiple factors to redefine uncertainty from a multi-facet view and calls for new metrics that credit not just correlation but the informativeness of signals in agentic scaffolding, which remains unexplored.
Parent UQ research should move towards more realistic setups featuring interactive long-horizon task episodes requiring sequential dynamics models over point-wise estimates. The proposed framework can be misused by adversaries to steer agents or manipulate uncertainty thresholds, so we recommend alleviations such as limiting exposure and monitoring for abuse.
